stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> CANDIDATE: G0 a design partner needs the state, or the roadmap calls it
    CANDIDATE --> SOURCING: G1 named analyst and reviewer assigned, watch sources registered
    SOURCING --> AUTHORING: G2 every V-09 field carries a state-primary gazette URL and date
    SOURCING --> BLOCKED_SOURCE: G3 a field has no primary source, or the gazette is unreadable
    BLOCKED_SOURCE --> SOURCING: G4 source found, or a counsel reading recorded
    BLOCKED_SOURCE --> DECLINED: G5 the state cannot be sourced this cycle
    AUTHORING --> CERTIFYING: G6 rule and due-date versions reviewed by the second qualified person
    CERTIFYING --> AUTHORING: G7 a golden or boundary case diverges
    CERTIFYING --> CAPTURE: G8 every case reproduces, including one boundary case per rule version
    CAPTURE --> PILOT: G9 portal and return flow captured in a Mode B first submission, runbooks published
    PILOT --> OFFERABLE: G10 one full live cycle filed and reconciled for a design partner
    PILOT --> AUTHORING: G11 the live cycle contradicts a drafted rule
    OFFERABLE --> MAINTAINED: G12 the state pack enters the normal watch and review cadence
    MAINTAINED --> DEGRADED: G13 a watch source goes silent, or a runbook passes its re-verify date
    DEGRADED --> MAINTAINED: G14 source restored and the runbook re-verified
    DEGRADED --> WITHDRAWN: G15 the state cannot be maintained - tenants move to computation plus carve-out
    DECLINED --> [*]
    WITHDRAWN --> [*]

    note right of CANDIDATE
      No tenant is offered a state before
      OFFERABLE. Liability still computes
      and shows, with the reason no
      session is offered.
    end note

    note right of CAPTURE
      Aggregator tables never seed a rule
      row or a runbook. A portal banner is
      a lead to verify, not a source.
    end note

    note left of DEGRADED
      Degradation is visible to the tenant
      through the coverage statement, and
      the obligation keeps its deadline
      clock whatever our state.
    end note
